@@ -1,5 +1,31 @@
 # Distant Horizons: accept Demonica as the Iris provider
 
+## Local compatibility backport for DH 3.3.3
+
+This local 0.7.3 build backports `MixinAbstractModInitializer` and its mixin
+configuration from Demonica v0.8.1. It keeps Demonica 0.7.3's Cleanroom 0.6.12/0.6.13
+support and exact Celeritas pin unchanged. The only other backport selects
+CodeChickenLib 3.3.8's published `dev` classifier after its POM changed on
+2026-10-15. No other 0.8.x runtime changes are included.
+
+The same local build also hardens LittleTiles transition caches: their existing
+cache monitor now covers `get`, `hasAdditional`, `beforeUpdate` and `afterUpdate`;
+`combine` uses duplicate input-buffer cursors; the Demonica bridge holds manager
+then cache locks throughout vertex copying. This preserves the existing lock order
+and does not alter cached geometry, vertex formats or Celeritas's pinned JAR.
+
+DH 3.3.3 renamed its entry point from `cleanroom.CleanroomMain` to
+`forge112.ForgeMain`, so the original 0.7.3 mixin silently stopped applying.
+The backported hook targets DH's shared `AbstractModInitializer`, handles both
+provider-registration overloads, and registers Demonica's Iris accessor once.
+Regression tests cover the released `actinium` provider, a future second
+`demonica` registration, array registration and unrelated compatibility accessors.
+
+Upstream implementation:
+https://github.com/ndellagrotte/Demonica/blob/v0.8.1/src/main/java/com/demonica/mixin/mod/distanthorizons/MixinAbstractModInitializer.java
+
+The original design notes below describe the superseded 0.7.3 hook.
+
 Draft of an issue for Distant Horizons, not sent. Whether and when to send it is the
 maintainer's decision.
 
